PURPOSE

The Engine is, and always will be, free and open source. Nobody may take
it, modify it, and sell a closed version of it. At the same time, the
people who build presentation assets for a wiki should be able to earn
money from their work. This Exception draws that line.

1. DEFINITIONS

   "Engine" means the NotAnotherWiki Engine source code, including all of
   its Rust crates, its templates, its migrations, and its build scripts,
   as distributed by the project.

   "Extension Interface" means the documented, runtime mechanisms by which
   the Engine loads external assets: the skin loader, the template and
   module resolvers, the component host bindings, the plugin host, and any
   other interface explicitly designated as an extension point by the
   project documentation.

   "Covered Asset" means any of the following that you create:

     a. a skin or theme, including its layouts, stylesheets, fonts, and
        image assets;
     b. a page in the Template namespace, or an equivalent markup
        template;
     c. a page in the Module namespace, or an equivalent component;
     d. a plugin loaded through the plugin host;

   provided in every case that the asset:

     i.   is loaded by the Engine at runtime through an Extension
          Interface;
     ii.  does not modify, patch, replace, subclass at the source level,
          or statically link against any part of the Engine; and
     iii. does not alter the behaviour of the Engine by changing its
          source code, its configuration schema, or its database schema.

   "Derivative Work of the Engine" means any work based on the Engine or
   on any modification of the Engine's source, other than a Covered Asset.

